Subject: [PATCH] nuway_can / nuway_rviz_plugin: declare the deps they actually use

Both CMakeLists call find_package on packages their package.xml never
declares, so colcon has no dependency edge and schedules them before those
packages are built. On a clean workspace the build fails at configure time:

  nuway_can:         By not providing "Findautoware_utils_diagnostics.cmake" ...
  nuway_rviz_plugin: By not providing "Findautoware_adapi_v1_msgs.cmake" ...

Both dependencies are present in the workspace and build fine - only the
ordering is wrong. The failure does not show up in the Docker image, where
these packages are already installed before the build starts.

Upstream: uwa-rev/canbridge_cpp @ autoware. Carry this until it is fixed there.
---
diff --git nuway_can/package.xml nuway_can/package.xml
index 2bd650a..b2e03fd 100644
--- nuway_can/package.xml
+++ nuway_can/package.xml
@@ -23,6 +23,10 @@
   <depend>nuway_interfaces</depend>
   <depend>joy_linux</depend>
   <depend>teleop_twist_joy</depend>
+  <depend>autoware_utils_diagnostics</depend>
+  <depend>autoware_vehicle_msgs</depend>
+  <depend>autoware_adapi_v1_msgs</depend>
+  <depend>tier4_vehicle_msgs</depend>
 
   <test_depend>ament_lint_auto</test_depend>
   <test_depend>ament_lint_common</test_depend>
diff --git nuway_rviz_plugin/package.xml nuway_rviz_plugin/package.xml
index eb9abcc..246859a 100644
--- nuway_rviz_plugin/package.xml
+++ nuway_rviz_plugin/package.xml
@@ -14,6 +14,12 @@
   <depend>geometry_msgs</depend>
   <depend>ament_index_cpp</depend>
   <depend>nlohmann_json</depend>
+  <depend>autoware_adapi_v1_msgs</depend>
+  <depend>pluginlib</depend>
+  <depend>rviz_common</depend>
+  <depend>lifecycle_msgs</depend>
+  <depend>std_msgs</depend>
+  <depend>qtbase5-dev</depend>
 
   <test_depend>ament_lint_auto</test_depend>
   <test_depend>ament_lint_common</test_depend>
